// MathNet Problem: 0agx
@Competition: XV-th Junior Balkan Mathematical Olympiad
@Topic: Geometry > Plane Geometry > Combinatorial Geometry

// State space for mathematical reasoning
State(4096) → reasoning_space
WaveState(2048) → solution_wave

// Problem: Let $n > 3$ be a positive integer. An equilateral triangle $ABC$ is divided into $n^2$ identical equilateral "small" triangles using lines parallel to its sides. The figure below illustrates the case ...

// Apply reasoning transform
reasoning_space @ W_initial >> LayerNorm

// Attention over solution candidates
Attention(query=reasoning_space, memory=solution_wave)

// Entropy gate to collapse to correct solution
⊕EntropyGate(threshold=0.3)

// Answer: 3(2n - 3)
